{"repositoryId":1310014869,"availability":"available","full":"iximiuz/shellgym","name":"shellgym","description":"ShellGym - an Interactive Linux Command-Line Trainer","category":"Education","language":"Go","stars":430,"forks":38,"created":"2026-07-23T14:11:41Z","updated":"2026-10-01T13:45:27Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://labs.iximiuz.com/playgrounds/shellgym","topics":["learning-by-doing","linux","shell","trainer"],"demo":"https://labs.iximiuz.com/playgrounds/shellgym","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.501Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.501Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.501Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.501Z","stars":430,"forks":38}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["ShellGym is a background daemon with a built-in web UI that turns any Linux box into an interactive command-line trainer.","\"Learn the idea in a tutorial. Build the reflex in ShellGym.\"","Tutorials explain concepts - ShellGym drills them, helping you form the right muscle memory. Open a split-screen: a completely ordinary terminal on the one side, and the ShellGym UI on the other. The UI shows small, fast-changing assignments - reps (in the traditional gym sense). Each rep asks for one concrete action (enter a directory, create a file, kill a process, free a port) and completes automatically the moment the system state changes. There is no \"check\" button and no copy-paste: you will have to type real commands into a real shell, and the gym trainer will observe your actions and…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/iximiuz/shellgym/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b02da8da210012914cfd25c942141257a9f59844b265002b366f2dae1ad4a628","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.617Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:05.617Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"ShellGym is a background daemon with a built-in web UI that turns any Linux box into an int